Also I should specify the "conditional-response (kicked ensemble) test": initialize from frames where the mode is displaced from its conditional mean, generate many rollouts, compute ensemble-conditional mean relaxation E[x(t)|x_0] and check it oscillates at the reference frequency with the reference damping. This is a strong time-domain statistical measure of fast dynamics. Good primary/secondary candidate. Actually maybe this should be the PRIMARY endpoint since it's phase-free (ensemble mean over rollouts starting from same x0) — a deterministic, model-discriminating quantity. Hmm, but phase coherence across rollouts from the same x0 is well-defined and reference-like: the ensemble-conditional mean of the *reference* trajectory ensemble conditioned on x0 shows ringing that decays with T2. And a model with no fast dynamics gives a monotone non-oscillatory relaxation. That's a beautiful primary endpoint. It's "conditional-mean response fidelity" ρ_ring or "ringing recovery".

